                    7. Translating powers into cards
   For those readers interested in the games of SET and EvenQuads,
we explain how to translate these results into specific codes for cards.
First, we need a primitive root g of F×         q and its minimal polynomial
over Fp . For SET, it is easy to verify that g 4 − g − 1 is irreducible
over F3 . By applying the Division Algorithm to find the remainder
after division by g 4 − g − 1, each power g k may be uniquely written as
g k = c1 g 3 + c2 g 2 + c3 g + c4 for cj ∈ F3 . These coefficients (c1 , c2 , c3 , c4 )
8        ANTHONY KABLE, MELISSA MILLS, AND DAVID J. WRIGHT

give the coordinates of the corresponding card. It turns out that a root
g of g 4 − g − 1 has order 80 and thus the powers g k give all 80 nonzero
elements. Below is a table of codes for the cap sets of cosets modulo
G81,20 . In each 4 × 5 block, the exponent k increases across each row
and then down to the next row from 0 to 19.


                   g 4k                                g 4k+1
